# What does NOT ship. Wrangler reads this as a .gitignore-style denylist.
#
# Why this file exists: with assets.directory "./" Wrangler walks the whole working tree and
# does not respect .gitignore. The first dry-run read 8319 files and hard-failed on
# .venv-seg/.../llvmlite.dll at 115 MiB against the 25 MiB per-asset limit - so the deploy
# command fails outright, not merely uploading more than it should.
#
# What DOES ship (keep this list in mind before adding patterns): index.html, 404.html,
# assets/css, assets/js, assets/fonts, the images under assets/img, favicon.png,
# apple-touch-icon.png, og-image.png, robots.txt, sitemap.xml - and _headers, which Wrangler
# parses rather than serves, so it must stay in the assets directory.

# The segmentation venv for tools/cutout.py: ~400 MB, and the direct cause of the failure.
.venv-seg/

# Local verification output, never part of the site.
_shots/
_lowpoly/

# Tooling and VCS state.
.git/
.gitignore
.wrangler/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/

# Generator scripts and the raw inputs they work from. None of it is reachable from the two
# HTML files; the derived assets they produce (me-duotone.webp, ckad-credly-transparent.webp)
# are what ships. Excluding them here keeps them in git for regeneration - the deploy is the
# only thing they are kept out of.
tools/
me.jpg
assets/img/badges/ckad-credly.png
assets/img/badges/ckad-credly-transparent.png

# Repo meta and local reports.
LICENSE
*.md
lighthouse*.json
wrangler.jsonc
